      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am not convinced there to be a bug. The Quest 2 is a system with 6 GB RAM which meets the bare minimum system requirements. 2 GB of that RAM is reserved for the Meta Horizon OS. That leaves little room for VRChat, avatars and the world.\n\nYou seem to imply that you are constantly toggling between \"show avatar\" and either the safety shield or \"hide avatar\" setting, possibly in an effort to load Very Poor rated avatars on mobile platforms. Have you considered... possibly not doing that to avoid harming yourself, on an aging Quest 2 platform that's already redlining on performance?\n\nBased on the above assumption, it seems like the feature of not loading more avatars is working as intended to prevent the client from outright crashing on you from low memory conditions.",
